---
title: Crispy Duck
source: Nigella Express <urn:isbn:9780701181840>
author: Nigella Lawson
servings: 4
course: Starter
prep time: 30m
cook time: 4h30m
locale: en_GB
difficulty: Medium
cuisine: Chinese
tags:
- chinese
- savoury
- starter
- main-course
---

Preheat the oven to 170°C.

Cut off the flap of fat that hangs over the @duck{1}'s cavity. Sit the trimmed duck on a rack or slotted tray over a deep roasting tin and roast for ~{4%hours}.

Increase the oven temperature to 220°C and give a final ~{30%minutes} of intense heat.

> Alternatively just leave the duck in the low oven for a total of 5½ hours.

Sit @Chinese pancakes{30} on the top part of a steamer to cook or simply follow the instructions on the packet.

Carefully take the duck, in its tin, out of the oven. Transfer the duck to a board, shred it, using two forks to pull the meat apart, and set it on the table with the @hoisin or Peking duck sauce{1%jar}(270 ml), pancakes, @cucumber{0.5}(cut into matchsticks), and @spring onions{6}(cut into short strips) shreds, so everyone can make their own pancake parcels.